<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    NotesMap entitlements.

    Deliberately empty under the Hardened Runtime. Rationale:

    -   App Sandbox is NOT enabled. The app must read the Apple Notes
        SQLite store at
        ~/Library/Group Containers/group.com.apple.notes/NoteStore.sqlite
        which lives in another app's group container. Sandboxed apps
        cannot reach this path; only Apple itself can grant the entitlement.
        We rely on macOS's per-folder Full Disk Access prompt instead, the
        user explicitly grants the app access in System Settings → Privacy
        & Security → Full Disk Access.

    -   Hardened Runtime is enabled (project.yml: ENABLE_HARDENED_RUNTIME).
        With no entitlements, the runtime blocks the dangerous defaults:
        -   no JIT (com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit)
        -   no unsigned executable memory
        -   no library validation bypass
        -   no DYLD env var hijacking
        -   no executable page protection bypass
        -   no debugger attachment in shipped builds

    -   Network access: the app only talks to http://localhost:11434
        (Ollama, optional, for AI labels and embeddings). Without sandbox,
        macOS cannot scope this further, but the only network code paths
        live in EmbeddingService.swift and OllamaLabelService.swift, both
        hardcoded to localhost.

    Adding ANY key below means weakening this posture. Do not add entries
    casually, prefer adjusting the architecture so the entitlement isn't
    needed.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
